      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{623e71d45e8530528588418a|full_name} I could see that still being fatiguing for some users, but it could work. It definitely gives control to the user.\n\nI was thinking something more akin of a curve where it starts slower, but it gets faster.\n\nTo explain it further: When the user starts turning, the first turn is instant, the second turn is the slowest, but the subsequent turns are a lot faster, until a point where it reaches maximum speed. This curve only needs to be slight enough to prevent that second turn to activate when the user didn't mean to.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
